          "@id": "https://marincountygov.github.io/marin-data/id/regulation/pmr-24"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://marincountygov.github.io/marin-data/id/regulation/pmr-4"
        }
      ],
      "legislationType": "regulation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://marincountygov.github.io/marin-data/id/regulation/pmr-3/3.3",
      "@type": "Legislation",
      "legislationIdentifier": "3.3",
      "name": "Commission Meetings",
      "codificationLevel": "section",
      "position": 3,
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://marincountygov.github.io/marin-data/id/regulation/pmr-3"
      },
      "text": "A. The Personnel Commission will meet at least once each calendar quarter and on the call of the Chair or of three members of the Commission.\n\nB. All meetings will be held in the Administration Building of the Frank Lloyd Wright Civic Center, San Rafael, California, or such other place as may be determined by the Commission.\n\nC. All meetings of the Commission will be open and public except and unless an executive session is legally authorized or as otherwise set forth herein. All persons will be permitted to attend any open public meeting of the Commission.\n\nD. Except as otherwise provided herein, Robert’s Rules of Order will guide the Commission in its proceedings.\n\nE. Three members of the Commission will constitute a quorum and the concurrence of three members present at the meeting will be necessary to take any action.\n\nF. An Agenda with accompanying materials pertinent to items to be brought before the Commission will be in the hands of individual Commissioners at least seventy-two hours in advance of the meeting date.\n\nG. The deadline for communications to the Personnel Commission is established at the close of business seven days in advance of the meeting date. Communications and requests to the Commission, insofar as practicable, shall be in writing. Communications and requests to the Commission should be directed to the Executive Secretary, Marin County Personnel Commission, Human Resources Department, Civic Center, San Rafael, California, 94903. Individuals may personally request time or consideration of any item not on the agenda by the Commission at any meeting during the period designated as Open Time on the agenda or by the Chairperson.\n\nH. The Executive Secretary, or designee, shall record in the minutes, the time and place of each meeting, the names of the Commissioners present, all official acts of the Commission and the vote of the Commissioners. The minutes shall be written and presented for correction and approval at a regular meeting of the Commission as soon as possible. The minutes are public records and shall be open to public inspection.",
      "legislationType": "regulation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://marincountygov.github.io/marin-data/id/regulation/pmr-3/3.4",
      "@type": "Legislation",
      "legislationIdentifier": "3.4",
      "name": "Affirmative Action Advisory Committee",
      "codificationLevel": "section",
      "position": 4,
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://marincountygov.github.io/marin-data/id/regulation/pmr-3"
      },
      "text": "A. Establishment. By direction of the Board of Supervisors and action of the Personnel Commission, an Affirmative Action Advisory Committee will be appointed by the Personnel Commission for the purpose of continuous monitoring of the County’s affirmative action program and efforts, the consideration and development of recommendations to the Personnel Commission for policy improvements or specific areas of improvement to enhance the affirmative action program, and to carry out such other responsibilities as the Personnel Commission may assign to the Committee.\n\nB. Term. Committee members will serve two-year terms, and may apply to the Personnel Commission for re-appointment at the end of the term.\n\nC. Quorum. The presence of a majority of the members occupying seats on the committee shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of business.",
      "legislationType": "regulation"
    },
    {
